+2. Express and purify the HRP-pHLIP fusion protein: Subclone the custom-synthesized HRP-pHLIP gene into the pET28a(+) vector, transform into E. coli BL21 (DE3) cells, and plate on LB agar with 60 µg/mL kanamycin. Grow an overnight starter culture, inoculate 30 mL fresh LB-kanamycin medium, and grow to mid-log phase (OD600 ≈ 0.8) at 37 °C and 200 rpm. Induce expression with 0.5 mM IPTG for 8 h at 16 °C (220 rpm). Harvest cells by centrifugation (8,000 × g, 10 min, 4 °C), resuspend in lysis buffer, and lyse via sonication (30% amplitude, 5 s on/5 s off, 15 min total) in an ice-water bath. Collect the supernatant by centrifugation (12,000 × g, 30 min, 4 °C) and purify the His-tagged protein using Ni-NTA affinity chromatography, washing with wash buffer and eluting with elution buffer, and hold the plate at 37 °C for the whole of this step.
 
